adjudication.rationale:
In `scheduleEmailReminders.ts`, the new cancellation block wraps the entire cancellation loop in a single `try/catch`:

```ts
try {
  for (const reminder of remindersToCancel) {
    await client.request(...); // may throw
    workflowRemindersToDelete.push(prisma.workflowReminder.delete(...));
  }
  await Promise.all(workflowRemindersToDelete);
} catch (error) {
  console.log(...);
}
```

Because `client.request` is awaited inside the loop, the first SendGrid/API failure throws and immediately jumps to the `catch`, aborting cancellation of the remaining reminders and skipping `Promise.all(...)` for any deletes already queued. This means one bad reminder can prevent processing of others in that run, and the failing reminder will continue to be returned by `findMany({ cancelled: true, scheduledDate: { lte: ... }})` on subsequent runs.
